  "note": "Fresh repositories only: v0.43.0 empty Bootstrap cannot reliably erase legacy backup peers. Allocated Kubo A/B stay online for Cluster connector APIs, without Kubo swarm listeners/discovery/routing/telemetry, behind a mandatory Docker internal network. ProviderPhase adds a third independent source with these same settings and daemon --offline; it is never an allocation and is stopped before target local-read verification. RelayClient=false alone does not disable the virtual /p2p-circuit listener: Network.Relay=false is required and read back. DisableNatPortMap=true disables NAT mapping; AutoConf placeholders are removed. Default mode preserves the previously accepted single-block verifier case; ProviderPhase never preloads either target and covers Proxy+REST CAR/upload, genuine crypto stored bytes, original reachable full DAG/bytes, fresh REST 2/2, no-fallback mismatch and CID-only re-pin after source stop. Negative CAR/source-failure contracts are local HTTP faults, not real N/N evidence. Not complete Stage6/worker/S3/auth/account/continuous availability. Proxy add uses Name/Hash/Bytes/Size (Size string), REST uses name/cid/bytes/size/allocations (size number); never translate real wire. No public network, reused volumes, pin/rm, unpin or GC."
